  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We all have those moments when someone has to be pulled aside for a quick, private conversation. Leaving the world you are in and comming back is annoying, and sending a private message is difficult in VR, so what do you do? You pull them to a space in the map that no one is in, outside of proximity volume. It never fails that someone has to follow, so you ether have to ask them to give you some alone time, leave the world anyway, or do a private message through a messaging app.\n\nI know an easy way to fix this. Add an option on the main menu to drop a private room. When the button is mashed, a door spawns in front of who requested it. System-wise, a code is randomly generated, the code is attached to the door and to the player who spawned it who is also labeled as that door's master. The Master asks the player they need to speak to to grab the door, or they are invited through the private room menu that only list local players. When the door is grabbed a menu pops up asking the master if they allow that player in as a guest with yes or no. On accepted invite/guest, the random code is attached to the guest and both the master and any guest can enter and exit as needed. This gives the ability to have more than one guest in the private room. On enter, anyone with the code fully hides and mutes anyone without it, and vice versa for everyone without the code. The room is destroyed when the master chooses the option in their menu, the master leaves the world, or everyone leaves the private room. \n\nThe door could be just a base model, low poly door for ease of access, and so guest don't have to go in their menus. It's also aesthetically pleasing. Heck you could make it where people could customize their own doors through the sdk. Could be an easy first step to learning avatar creation. I honestly think this would be a great idea, and it would make conversing with people easier. Leaving a world with someone, to tell them one sentence about something you don't want anyone else to hear, is just a pain. It would also help for afk moments, and for people that get overwhelmed by a lot of noise and need a quick break.\n\nJust think about it. No pressure.\nMystery",
